{"slug":"balanced-parentheses-list","title":"Generate the Balanced Brackets","topic":"backtracking","difficulty":"easy","order":417,"tags":["backtracking","strings","parentheses"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Count what is open, and never close more than you opened","body":["A string of brackets is balanced if every `(` is closed by a later `)` and no `)` comes before its `(`. Build the string from left to right and remember two numbers: how many `(` and how many `)` were placed so far. There are exactly two rules:","- an opening bracket may be added while fewer than `n` were used;\n- a closing bracket may be added only while there are more `(` than `)` in the string, so that every `)` has an open bracket to close.",{"code":"def build(n, opened, closed, current, out):\n    if len(current) == 2 * n:\n        out.append(\"\".join(current))\n        return\n    if opened < n:\n        current.append(\"(\")\n        build(n, opened + 1, closed, current, out)\n        current.pop()\n    if closed < opened:\n        current.append(\")\")\n        build(n, opened, closed + 1, current, out)\n        current.pop()"},"Because the rules are checked at every step, **every** string that is started can be finished, and no unbalanced string is ever built. In the ASCII table `(` comes before `)`, so trying `(` first produces the strings in dictionary order. The number of strings is the Catalan number (1430 for `n = 8`)."]},"statement":["Print all balanced strings made of `n` pairs of brackets `(` and `)`, in dictionary order (where `(` is smaller than `)`), one per line."],"inputFormat":["The only line has `n`."],"outputFormat":["All balanced strings in dictionary order, one per line."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 8"],"examples":[{"input":"3\n","output":"((()))\n(()())\n(())()\n()(())\n()()()\n","note":"The five strings are ((())), (()()), (())(), ()(()) and ()()()."}],"hints":["Remember how many opening and closing brackets are used so far.","You may add ( if fewer than n opening brackets were used.","You may add ) only if the string has more ( than )."],"starter":{"python":"n = int(input())\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["The string is built left to right. `(` is allowed while fewer than `n` were used and `)` while it has an open bracket to close. Trying `(` first gives dictionary order."],"complexity":"Time O(Catalan(n) * n), space O(n) besides the output.","code":{"python":"def build(n, opened, closed, current, out):\n    if len(current) == 2 * n:\n        out.append(\"\".join(current))\n        return\n    if opened < n:\n        current.append(\"(\")\n        build(n, opened + 1, closed, current, out)\n        current.pop()\n    if closed < opened:\n        current.append(\")\")\n        build(n, opened, closed + 1, current, out)\n        current.pop()\n\nn = int(input())\n\nout = []\nbuild(n, 0, 0, [], out)\nprint(\"\\n\".join(out))\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nvoid build(int n, int opened, int closed, string& current, vector<string>& out) {\n    if ((int)current.size() == 2 * n) {\n        out.push_back(current);\n        return;\n    }\n    if (opened < n) {\n        current.push_back('(');\n        build(n, opened + 1, closed, current, out);\n        current.pop_back();\n    }\n    if (closed < opened) {\n        current.push_back(')');\n        build(n, opened, closed + 1, current, out);\n        current.pop_back();\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n\n    vector<string> out;\n    string current;\n    build((int)n, 0, 0, current, out);\n    for (const string& s : out) cout << s << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static void build(int n, int opened, int closed, StringBuilder current, List<String> out) {\n        if (current.length() == 2 * n) {\n            out.add(current.toString());\n            return;\n        }\n        if (opened < n) {\n            current.append('(');\n            build(n, opened + 1, closed, current, out);\n            current.deleteCharAt(current.length() - 1);\n        }\n        if (closed < opened) {\n            current.append(')');\n            build(n, opened, closed + 1, current, out);\n            current.deleteCharAt(current.length() - 1);\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n\n        List<String> out = new ArrayList<>();\n        build((int) n, 0, 0, new StringBuilder(), out);\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        for (String s : out) sb.append(s).append(\"\\n\");\n        System.out.print(sb);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"1\n","output":"()\n"},{"input":"2\n","output":"(())\n()()\n"},{"input":"3\n","output":"((()))\n(()())\n(())()\n()(())\n()()()\n"},{"input":"4\n","output":"(((())))\n((()()))\n((())())\n((()))()\n(()(()))\n(()()())\n(()())()\n(())(())\n(())()()\n()((()))\n()(()())\n()(())()\n()()(())\n()()()()\n"},{"input":"5\n","output":"((((()))))\n(((()())))\n(((())()))\n(((()))())\n(((())))()\n((()(())))\n((()()()))\n((()())())\n((()()))()\n((())(()))\n((())()())\n((())())()\n((()))(())\n((()))()()\n(()((())))\n(()(()()))\n(()(())())\n(()(()))()\n(()()(()))\n(()()()())\n(()()())()\n(()())(())\n(()())()()\n(())((()))\n(())(()())\n(())(())()\n(())()(())\n(())()()()\n()(((())))\n()((()()))\n()((())())\n()((()))()\n()(()(()))\n()(()()())\n()(()())()\n()(())(())\n()(())()()\n()()((()))\n()()(()())\n()()(())()\n()()()(())\n()()()()()\n"},{"input":"6\n","output"